readme.text:
Measured behaviour (the full matrix is under `## Security posture`): workspace writes allowed; **writes** outside the policy denied;
outbound network blocked by default; clipboard isolated from the host. Reads are **not** an absolute boundary — see the
security-posture notes below before trusting a machine. Three tier-dependent facts are worth knowing:

In order of precedence:

1. plugin `config.wxcExecPath` (absolute path to `wxc-exec.exe`);
2. environment variable `DSH_MXC_WXC`;
3. derivation from an installed `@microsoft/mxc-sdk`: `<package>/bin/<arch>/wxc-exec.exe` (the SDK's own
   layout — `arm64` on Arm64 hosts, `x64` elsewhere), then `<package>/bin/wxc-exec.exe` (older layout).
